<newsitem itemid="22999" id="root" date="1996-08-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Hambro Countrywide moves to H1 pretax profit.</title>
<headline>Hambro Countrywide moves to H1 pretax profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		2.41		   vs 1.92 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.5		    vs nil</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    10.5		   vs 5.8 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Estate agency and financial products group Hambro Countrywide Plc said a return to profitability had produced a positive cash flow and enabled it to pay an interim dividend of 0.5 pence per share net. It said a significant improvement in trading and market share had led to the return to profit.  </p>
<p> Turnover		   91.1		   vs 73.7</p>
<p> Operating profit	 10.78		  vs 5.61 loss</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.405		  vs 0.124</p>
<p> Profit on disposal     0.172		  vs nil</p>
<p> Tax paid		   2.02		   vs 0.96</p>
<p> Net taxed		  8.52		   vs 6.78 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 21, 1996</p>
<p> Div  registration date September 17, 1996</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 9, 1996</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
